  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Scorer off – 3 v 3 with a player up or down",
  "description": "Two teams with two or three lines of three each. Play 3 v 3 on the full court or a smaller court across, with goalkeepers in both goals. The subs wait by the boards.\n\nWhoever scores leaves the court at once, and the team plays on a player short. The goalkeeper of the team that conceded restarts at once with a throw-out. Shifts are short, about 30 seconds, then the next three from each team come on and it starts again at 3 v 3. If a team scores three goals in one shift it has no one left on the court and the shift is over. The goals count for the whole match.\n\nVariant: move the goals closer together so the shots come quicker.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "With an extra player: move the ball quickly and find the free player."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Decide quickly between shot and pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A player down: stay tight in front of your own goal and close the shooting lanes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Come on straight away at a change – no dead time."
    }
  ],
